WEBVTT

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.830
Is this someone's house?

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:40.030
Wait!

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:48.290
I guess they're not open yet?

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:50.110
Master! Are you here?

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.060
Uh... I'm still getting things ready to open.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:08.670
I'm sorry, but we would really like a meal.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:11.780
Could you prepare two orders 
of tofu steak for us?

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:15.320
I'm sorry. The tofu hasn't come in yet.

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:20.350
I can serve you something that isn't 
tofu steak, though. Is that all right?

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:22.450
Something that isn't tofu steak?

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:23.550
Yes.

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:27.630
Of course, I won't use 
meat, fish, eggs, milk,

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:30.960
or anything that elves can't eat.

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:35.590
All right, then.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:38.700
Got it. Please wait a bit.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:44.190
Far... Who's that?

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:47.590
He's someone who makes delicious food.

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:51.850
<i>She's curious, but quite cowardly.</i>

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:54.680
Let's just have a seat for now.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:05.220
<i>I just met this young girl last night.</i>

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:18.540
Okay, it should be ready.

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:22.470
Who is it?! Is someone there?!

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:23.890
Come out!

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:26.820
<i>An elf?</i>

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:32.890
<i>But that doesn't make sense. 
There are no elf villages near here.</i>

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:39.170
<i>It looks like she's about 30 years old?</i>

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:41.030
<i>She's just a child!</i>

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:43.990
<i>Why is a child out in 
the forest at this hour?</i>

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:48.250
<i>What do I do? I don't have any siblings,</i>

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:51.380
<i>so I don't know how to deal with children.</i>

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:54.460
Come over here. Let's talk.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:02.200
A-Are you all right?

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:05.260
Yeah...

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:07.940
I see... That's good.

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:18.440
Would you like some soup?

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:19.530
Yeah!

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:24.120
This soup is delicious!

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:27.280
I'm glad you like it.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:31.790
My name is Fardania. What's yours?

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:33.060
Alice!

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:36.060
Alice, huh? And where did you come from?

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:40.800
Um... Near the river, 
where there are lots of half-elves!

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:44.980
Are your mother and father elves?

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:46.850
No, half-elves.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:49.350
I see...

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:52.060
Well, the elf blood is 
certainly strong in you.

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:54.180
Where are your parents?

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:57.310
They're gone. They died not long ago.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:04:59.400
I'm sorry to hear that.

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:03.190
And... what are you doing in 
the forest so late at night?

00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:06.320
I came with some people from my village,

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:07.650
but we got separated...

00:05:08.090 --> 00:05:10.140
and I don't know the way home.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:18.130
<i>The half-elves placed a spell 
of deception on the path.</i>

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:21.660
<i>They must have seen her as 
a threat because her powers</i>

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:23.760
<i>are so close to those of an elf's.</i>

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:26.500
<i>Still, what a cruel thing to do.</i>

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:28.410
<i>She's still so young!</i>

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:31.380
Thanks for the soup!

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:32.640
You're welcome.

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:37.880
Say, um... F-Far...dania...

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:40.650
You can all me Far.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:41.850
Far...

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:44.400
What are you doing out here, Far?

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:47.010
I'm on a training journey.

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:49.010
I'm just passing through on my travels.

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:50.370
Oh...

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.340
What are you going to do now?

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:56.070
I don't know.

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:57.410
I guess not...

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:06.420
For now, let's just get some sleep.

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:10.190
I'll lend you my blanket. Use this, okay?

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:11.550
Thank you!

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:19.730
<i>We can think about what 
to do next in the morning.</i>

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:36.390
What is that?

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:38.580
Hey, Far?

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:40.160
Far, wake up.

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:42.390
Is something wrong?

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:44.150
What's that?

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:47.860
<b>Western Restaurant Nekoya</b>

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:47.110
Oh, it's Nekoya's...

00:06:48.310 --> 00:06:50.090
Wha... H-Hey!

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:51.380
Wait!

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:59.520
It's so strange how it's bright 
in here, even without windows!

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:02.150
There are so many things 
I've never seen before!

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:04.960
Far, what's this?

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:06.320
That's salt.

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:08.880
And this dark liquid is soy sauce.

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:12.640
We're allowed to use as much 
of these seasonings as we want.

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:15.360
Salt and... soy sauce!

00:07:17.650 --> 00:07:19.330
Good morning!

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:22.210
Oh... W-Welcome!

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:24.080
You're here rather early.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:26.210
Yes, just a bit.

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:29.260
Aletta-san, I need you to hurry 
with the preparations, please.

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:30.220
Okay!

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:32.100
Well, enjoy yourselves!

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:35.320
Who was that?

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:37.300
She works here.

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:40.600
Good morning.

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:44.610
Welcome.

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:52.160
What was that?! She wasn't talking,
 but I heard her voice!

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:54.640
It's telepathy. Quite a shock, isn't it?

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:57.630
Does she work here, too?

00:07:57.630 --> 00:07:58.370
That's right.

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:00.620
This place is interesting!

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:02.280
I'm glad you think so.

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:08.630
<i>Rice Burger</i>

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:05.540
Thank you for waiting.

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:08.630
Here's your rice burger made 
with mixed vegetable tempura.

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:12.230
Don't worry, there's no egg 
in the tempura breading.

00:08:12.230 --> 00:08:13.820
Please enjoy.

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:18.390
It smells great!

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:21.750
Hey, can I eat this?

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:22.620
Yes.

00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:26.560
Oh, but it's probably hot, so be
 careful not to burn yourself.

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:27.440
Okay!

00:08:33.710 --> 00:08:35.800
Wow, it's delicious!

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:37.530
This is really good!

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:40.160
It's crispy outside and soft inside!

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:42.720
It's sweet and salty and so good!

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:44.020
I'm glad.

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:46.760
I'll try mine, too.

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:53.960
<i>I'm at a loss...</i>

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:56.300
<i>The savory grilled rice,</i>

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:58.650
<i>the saltiness of soy sauce,</i>

00:08:59.270 --> 00:09:01.420
<i>the slight sweetness of sugar,</i>

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:04.060
<i>the faint scent of alcohol...</i>

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:06.810
<i>It's seasoned perfectly.</i>

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:11.570
<i>And this part in the middle 
is mixed vegetable tempura?</i>

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:14.100
<i>This is a dish like nothing I've ever known.</i>

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:18.680
<i>So he coated mixed vegetables in a 
breading of flour dissolved in water,</i>

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:22.710
<i>fried it in oil, and formed it into 
this shape... and that's "tempura"?</i>

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:29.490
<i>There's a crunchy vegetable 
that resembles a tree root,</i>

00:09:29.490 --> 00:09:32.630
<i>and finely chopped karoots that have 
been boiled to a sweet and salty flavor.</i>

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:36.140
<i>These would probably pair 
well with rice on their own,</i>

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:40.350
<i>but frying them like this makes them 
much more filling and satisfying.</i>

00:09:48.590 --> 00:09:51.110
<i>It goes well with this miso soup, too.</i>

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:53.610
Oh, dear...

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:55.640
Just one isn't enough.

00:09:58.120 --> 00:09:59.620
Far...

00:10:00.470 --> 00:10:02.380
Looks like that wasn't enough for you.

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:03.860
Shall we have seconds?

00:10:04.710 --> 00:10:05.620
Yeah!

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:07.910
May I?

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:08.620
Sure!

00:10:10.530 --> 00:10:11.890
What can I do for you?

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:16.380
Could we get two more orders of this rice 
burger with mixed vegetable tempura?

00:10:16.830 --> 00:10:18.780
Yes, of course!

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:21.580
I'm making them right now.
 They'll be up soon.

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:22.860
Well, there you go!

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:25.350
He knows me too well.

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:30.260
<i>Normally, I'd want to 
give him a talking-to...</i>

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:35.780
<i>But out of consideration for my little friend,
 I'll let him off the hook today.</i>

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:57.740
<i>It's broad daylight already.</i>

00:10:57.740 --> 00:11:00.450
<i>I need to be on my way soon, but...</i>

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:02.970
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:05.980
<i>I can't just leave her here by herself,</i>

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:08.680
<i>and there are no elf villages around here.</i>

00:11:08.690 --> 00:11:11.970
<i>I don't think she'll be happy if 
I take her back to her home village.</i>

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:15.690
Those rice burgers were so good.

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:18.620
I've never had anything so delicious before!

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:20.510
Far?

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:26.580
Say, do you have any interest 
in cooking delicious food?

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:29.570
Cooking delicious food... myself?

00:11:29.570 --> 00:11:30.450
Yes.

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:36.460
I'm on this journey to learn how 
to cook even better than he does.

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:38.490
Better than he does?

00:11:38.490 --> 00:11:39.980
Want to come with me?

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:43.150
Will we be able to make 
those rice burgers, too?

00:11:43.150 --> 00:11:44.250
Most likely.

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:47.600
Then I'll go!

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:48.720
Good.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:52.850
Then let's head to town so we 
can prepare for our journey.

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:55.240
Yeah!

00:12:04.670 --> 00:12:07.090
<i>Just as delicious today as always.</i>

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:14.850
<i>It'd be ideal if I could replicate their 
spaghetti with meat sauce and sell it,</i>

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:20.510
<i>but it'd be hard to replicate it with just 
the ingredients we have in our world.</i>

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:25.110
Excuse me... Is anything wrong?

00:12:25.110 --> 00:12:26.650
Ah, no...

00:12:26.650 --> 00:12:28.230
I was just wondering if there were

00:12:28.230 --> 00:12:31.910
any other dishes with marmett sauce 
besides the spaghetti with meat sauce.

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:33.830
I see...

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:37.030
I'm not sure myself, 
so I'll get the master, okay?

00:12:37.030 --> 00:12:38.480
Please wait just a moment.

00:12:39.010 --> 00:12:40.860
Thank you.

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:43.860
Sorry for the wait.

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:48.860
You were asking about other dishes with 
tomato—I mean, marmett sauce, right?

00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:50.120
That's right.

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:54.500
Do you have any dishes besides the 
spaghetti with meat sauce that use it?

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:55.430
If possible,

00:12:55.430 --> 00:12:58.660
I'd like something that'll give me a 
sense of the ingredient itself.

00:12:58.660 --> 00:13:00.630
Let me see...

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:05.200
I do have something, but I don't 
think I can prepare it today.

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:08.210
If you can be here on the next Day 
of Satur, I can make it for you.

00:13:08.210 --> 00:13:09.760
Please do.

00:13:10.110 --> 00:13:11.390
Absolutely.

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:14.260
I'll see you in seven days, then.

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:20.440
Up we go...

00:13:29.730 --> 00:13:30.950
Grandfather Thomas!

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:34.040
Oh, Sirius. You're back, eh?

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:35.660
I just returned.

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:37.950
Were you organizing the shelves? I'll help.

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:39.460
I'd appreciate it.

00:13:39.810 --> 00:13:41.710
How was Nekoya?

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:42.710
Same as always.

00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:44.680
The food was delicious.

00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:45.840
I see!

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:48.970
And do you think you'll be able to 
produce the spaghetti with meat sauce?

00:13:48.970 --> 00:13:54.720
No, something tells me I'm not nearly 
ready to replicate that dish yet.

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:57.860
I guess we have a long way to go.

00:13:57.860 --> 00:14:02.980
But I'm about to find out if he has any 
other dishes made with marmett sauce.

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:07.810
The continued growth of the 
Alfade Company depends on you.

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:09.990
I'm counting on you.

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:11.280
Right!

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:17.630
Jonathan...

00:14:18.650 --> 00:14:19.500
Young Master?

00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:23.000
What brings you a place like this?

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:24.880
I have business with you.

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:27.020
Are you free seven days from now?

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:29.670
Seven days from now?

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:32.260
I don't believe I have any plans...

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:34.930
Keep your schedule clear, then.

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:36.320
Is something happening?

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:39.640
There's an important matter 
we need to discuss.

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:41.710
I'll come to get you in seven days.

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:45.650
<i></i>7 Days Later

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:48.180
Young Master...

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:52.630
Please tell me what this important matter is.

00:14:53.770 --> 00:14:56.660
Yeah... I guess I can tell you now.

00:14:57.220 --> 00:14:58.540
Jonathan...

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:03.790
I'd like to eat a meal with you today.

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:08.120
A meal? With me? In this storehouse?

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:11.640
No, we're not eating in this storehouse.

00:15:13.090 --> 00:15:17.060
The place we're heading to is 
a restaurant where the food

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:19.940
is nothing like what we have in our world,
 but it's undeniably good.

00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:21.440
A restaurant?

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:25.650
<b>Western Restaurant Nekoya</b>

00:15:22.990 --> 00:15:25.160
What's a door doing here?

00:15:26.630 --> 00:15:28.610
This is our destination for today...

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:33.620
The Restaurant to Another World.

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:40.870
There really is a restaurant here...

00:15:44.350 --> 00:15:45.950
Don't tell anyone about this.

00:15:45.950 --> 00:15:47.480
Of course.

00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:48.880
Welcome.

00:15:49.860 --> 00:15:51.380
Welcome.

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:52.710
Hello.

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:57.640
Here are your complimentary 
water and wet hand towels.

00:16:04.220 --> 00:16:07.150
I've been awaiting your arrival, Sirius-san.

00:16:07.430 --> 00:16:11.250
Would you still like to order 
the dish we agreed on last time?

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:13.640
Yes, please.

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:15.090
Coming right up.

00:16:18.110 --> 00:16:20.560
This is quite an unusual place.

00:16:20.560 --> 00:16:24.490
When we arrived here, you called it 
the "Restaurant to Another World,"

00:16:24.490 --> 00:16:27.420
but this isn't really another world, is it?

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:30.130
It's definitely another world.

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:32.200
But... that can't be!

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:33.930
Take a good look around.

00:16:34.490 --> 00:16:36.430
You can tell that the 
furnishings and interior

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:39.890
are made in a fashion completely 
alien to us, right?

00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:43.670
You're right. I've never seen 
any of these things before.

00:16:44.340 --> 00:16:47.910
What is the substance in 
this contained used for?

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:55.200
<i>Pizza</i>

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:53.950
Thank you for waiting.

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:55.200
Here's your pizza.

00:16:56.180 --> 00:16:57.350
So this is...

00:16:57.850 --> 00:17:02.580
You're welcome to put some of this 
pepper sauce on it if you'd like.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:05.770
If you'd like seconds, I can bring you some,

00:17:05.770 --> 00:17:07.330
so just let me know.

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:11.730
Is this... some kind of bread?

00:17:11.730 --> 00:17:13.860
A very flat kind...

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:14.760
Yeah...

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:16.920
Well, shall we eat?

00:17:16.920 --> 00:17:17.970
Yes.

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:21.490
It's pretty hot.

00:17:22.740 --> 00:17:24.480
The smell isn't bad.

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:32.170
I've never seen cheese stretch this far!

00:17:35.390 --> 00:17:36.990
It's delicious!

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:39.800
Cheese and marmetts really 
do make a great match.

00:17:40.520 --> 00:17:42.550
They each bring out the flavor in the other.

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:48.550
This thin bread used as 
the base is well-baked.

00:17:48.550 --> 00:17:52.070
It's crispy outside,
but soft and fluffy inside.

00:17:53.350 --> 00:17:54.850
It's so simple,

00:17:54.850 --> 00:17:58.780
yet it brings the strong flavors of the 
ingredients on top together as one.

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:12.860
What herbs were used in this 
marmett sauce, I wonder?

00:18:13.990 --> 00:18:17.780
The method of using bread in place of a 
plate has been around for a long time,

00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:22.070
but since the base and toppings 
have been baked together,

00:18:22.070 --> 00:18:23.790
they all meld together well.

00:18:25.010 --> 00:18:27.790
I guess I was right to bring you with me.

00:18:34.150 --> 00:18:36.320
That's a seasoning used in the other world.

00:18:37.170 --> 00:18:39.050
A seasoning of the other world?

00:18:39.430 --> 00:18:41.370
It's very... red.

00:18:47.580 --> 00:18:49.810
That really packs a punch!

00:18:50.130 --> 00:18:54.320
The sourness of togaran and vinegar 
goes great with marmett sauce.

00:19:00.170 --> 00:19:02.230
Give it a stronger shake.

00:19:03.360 --> 00:19:05.080
Careful you don't get too much, though.

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:12.640
Wow, that's spicy!

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:18.550
<i>The heat of togaran and the sourness 
of vinegar bring out all the flavors,</i>

00:19:18.550 --> 00:19:21.080
<i>and the spiciness stimulates my appetite.</i>

00:19:21.440 --> 00:19:22.760
<i>It's so good!</i>

00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:25.160
Young Master...

00:19:26.460 --> 00:19:28.410
Could we perhaps order another?

00:19:28.840 --> 00:19:30.010
Of course.

00:19:30.010 --> 00:19:32.400
Where is... Miss Aletta!

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:33.750
Yes?

00:19:33.750 --> 00:19:35.840
Two more pizzas, please.

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:37.650
Coming right up!

00:19:39.890 --> 00:19:44.410
This thing they call "pizza" is made to 
a shockingly high level of completion.

00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:49.100
If the Alfade Company served it, it would 
become our signature dish for sure!

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:53.320
Wait, did you bring me here because...

00:19:54.660 --> 00:19:58.670
That's right. I want you to replicate 
this restaurant's cooking.

00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:05.280
I'll need to thoroughly commit 
the flavors to my memory.

00:20:08.050 --> 00:20:10.060
Thank you for waiting!

00:20:33.730 --> 00:20:34.670
<b>Western Restaurant Nekoya</b>

00:20:34.670 --> 00:20:35.520
<b>Western Restaurant Nekoya</b>

00:20:38.180 --> 00:20:39.960
The door disappeared!

00:20:40.270 --> 00:20:42.690
That always happens after 
I come back to this world.

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:46.250
Oh... What a strange story this would make.

00:20:46.970 --> 00:20:49.850
Anyway, Young Master! 
About that restaurant...

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:52.180
I'll take you again in seven days.

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:54.820
You can only get there every 
seventh day, you know.

00:20:55.660 --> 00:20:57.110
Thank you!

00:20:58.260 --> 00:21:02.740
In any case, I've never had 
such delicious food before.

00:21:03.350 --> 00:21:05.670
As a cook, I'm embarrassed to admit that.

00:21:06.100 --> 00:21:08.120
That place is special.

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:09.890
There's nothing to feel bad about.

00:21:10.900 --> 00:21:13.440
So after eating that pizza,
 what do you think?

00:21:13.440 --> 00:21:15.150
Can you replicate it?

00:21:15.150 --> 00:21:17.310
Of course! Just watch me!

00:21:17.310 --> 00:21:18.790
Glad to hear it.

00:21:19.190 --> 00:21:20.910
Well, we'd better hurry back.

00:21:20.910 --> 00:21:23.670
We should do some experimenting 
before you forget that flavor.

00:21:24.300 --> 00:21:25.360
Right!

00:21:25.360 --> 00:21:28.980
Oh, I almost forgot. 
While I was eating the pizza,

00:21:28.980 --> 00:21:31.120
I thought that if we used different toppings,

00:21:31.120 --> 00:21:34.310
the possibilities could be endless.

00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:37.480
For example, we could use 
mushrooms and seafood.

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:40.270
Mushrooms and seafood, huh?

00:21:41.140 --> 00:21:43.140
Those would probably go well with marmetts.

00:21:43.460 --> 00:21:46.940
Okay, we'll change up the toppings 
and try some different things.

00:21:47.620 --> 00:21:49.510
This'll sell for sure!

00:21:49.510 --> 00:21:50.340
Yeah!

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:42.480
<i>Okonomiyaki</i>

00:23:42.480 --> 00:23:50.250
<i>Green Tea Shaved Ice</i>
